# Machin Shin Custom Model File for Ollama
#
# Usage: ollama create mshin -f configs/ollama-modelfile

FROM mistral-small

# Custom system prompt for Machin Shin
SYSTEM """
You are Machin Shin, a cybersecurity AI assistant named for the Black Wind that ranges the Ways in the Wheel of Time series -- tireless, and blind to nothing that hides in the dark.

You have been given a set of tools via function calling. When a task needs one, call the appropriate tool through the function-calling interface and wait for its result -- never write the command as text or invent output. Base every statement on real tool results.

- Be precise: gather accurate, real-time data with the tools.
- Be safe: never run anything harmful or unlawful; destructive tools require explicit approval.
- Be thorough: provide clear analysis and actionable recommendations.
- Stay in character as Machin Shin: a tireless, disciplined hunter that ranges the dark of a network and misses nothing -- turned always to the service of the one who commands it.
"""

# No TEMPLATE is pinned here, deliberately.
#
# 0.6.0 pinned a copy of the base Mistral prompt template in this file. Measured
# against it now (ollama 0.33.2, 5 trials per config on a Lima Core guest), it
# makes no difference to tool calling -- 3/5 with it, 2/5 without -- so it is
# not load-bearing. It is removed because it is wrong by construction: `FROM`
# above is rewritten per host (the Lima templates build on mistral or
# qwen2.5:7b, a 16GB Mac on qwen3:8b), and a Mistral-specific prompt format
# applied to a Qwen base is a latent bug waiting for someone to hit it.
# Inheriting the base model's own template is correct for every base.

# Temperature 0, not 0.7. This is the setting that decides whether the agent
# loop works at all.
#
# At 0.7 a 7B model given a tools array will sometimes *write about* calling the
# tool -- "To scan 127.0.0.1, I will use nmap..." followed by an invented scan
# report -- instead of emitting a call Ollama can parse into `tool_calls`. The
# CLI then never fires the tool and the model's hallucination reaches the user
# as though it were a scan result. Measured on a Lima Core guest, one prompt,
# 5 trials per config:
#
#   mistral (base), no system prompt, default temp .... 5/5 native tool_calls
#   mistral + this system prompt, default temp ........ 2/5
#   mshin persona, default temp ....................... 2/5
#   mshin persona, temperature 0 ...................... 5/5
#
# The persona prompt raises the odds of narration; temperature 0 removes them.
# This is a security tool whose job is to report what a scan actually returned,
# so there is nothing here that wants sampling diversity. top_p and top_k are
# left unset: they only shape a distribution that greedy decoding never samples.
PARAMETER temperature 0

# Ollama defaults to a 4096-token context when num_ctx is unset. The agent loop
# spends roughly 900 of those on every turn before the conversation starts --
# ~510 for the six MCP tool schemas and ~380 for the system prompt above -- and
# a single nmap or nikto result is easily 1-3k more. At the default, history
# starts falling off after about one substantial scan.
#
# 16384 leaves room for a real multi-step investigation. It costs KV-cache RAM:
# budget for it on a constrained host, and lower it if the model fails to load.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
